@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# Edge.js: OpenClaw `node:sqlite` binding
+
+| | | Remarks |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| **Status** | ▶️ | The pinned binding compiles and passes its native contract; Chromium/WASIX proof remains. |
+| **Severity** | High | The official OpenClaw Gateway stops before startup without a safe synchronous SQLite implementation. |
+
+## Issue
+
+The complete, integrity-verified `openclaw@2026.7.1-2` package graph reaches
+its unmodified Gateway startup path in Chromium through the self-contained
+QuickJS Edge.js WASIX build. After a diagnostic-only Node version label
+replacement exposes the next boundary, OpenClaw fails in
+`requireNodeSqlite()` because `require("node:sqlite")` has no usable
+`DatabaseSync` implementation.
+
+The release immediately constructs an in-memory database, executes
+`SELECT sqlite_version()`, and rejects SQLite versions affected by the
+WAL-reset corruption bug. The browser runtime therefore cannot claim Node
+24.15 compatibility merely by changing its version string.
+
+## Action Plan
+
+1. Add an optional, explicitly configured SQLite amalgamation dependency to
+   the Edge.js build rather than silently depending on a host SQLite library.
+2. Register a portable N-API `internalBinding("sqlite")` implementation and
+   expose the existing `lib/sqlite.js` builtin only when that dependency is
+   present.
+3. Implement the synchronous OpenClaw-reached surface: `DatabaseSync`,
+   `StatementSync`, positional and named binding, `exec`, `prepare`, `get`,
+   `all`, `run`, `iterate`, `columns`, read-only open, and close. Closing a
+   database must finalize all retained statements, matching Node's
+   `DatabaseSync` lifecycle and releasing exclusive WAL ownership.
+4. Compile a pinned SQLite 3.53.4 amalgamation into the QuickJS WASIX artifact
+   with extension loading disabled and column metadata enabled.
+5. Add focused Edge.js tests for module identity, SQLite version safety,
+   transactions, WAL checkpoint, persistence, bindings, result types, and
+   explicit extension-loading failure.
+6. Rebuild the self-contained WASIX artifact and run the exact unmodified
+   OpenClaw Gateway diagnostic in Chromium.
+7. Record the next boundary. Do not change the normal runtime's Node version
+   claim until the SQLite proof and the broader OpenClaw compatibility profile
+   both pass.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+With the complete official package mounted at `/openclaw`, the diagnostic
+Gateway invocation exits with:
+
+```text
+SQLite support is unavailable or unsafe in this Node runtime.
+```
+
+The stack begins in the unmodified artifact:
+
+```text
+requireNodeSqlite
+withOpenClawStateStartupMigrationCheckpointDatabase
+readStartupMigrationVersion
+runDoctorConfigPreflight
+```
+
+The current builtin catalog intentionally places `sqlite` in
+`cannot_be_required`, while `lib/sqlite.js` delegates directly to
+`internalBinding("sqlite")`.
+
+## Progress
+
+- The optional CMake surface rejects an incomplete amalgamation directory.
+- SQLite 3.53.4 is compiled into the binding with extension loading disabled,
+  column metadata enabled, DQS disabled, and no host SQLite dependency.
+- A native QuickJS Edge build passes the OpenClaw-reached surface for
+  `exec`, `prepare`, `get`, `all`, `run`, `iterate`, `columns`, positional and
+  named bindings, transactions, savepoints, WAL checkpointing, read-only
+  reopen, foreign keys, persistence, retained-statement finalization, and
+  rejection of duplicate close.
+- WASIX applies `locking_mode=EXCLUSIVE` before the first guest statement.
+  Wasmer's mounted virtual filesystem cannot provide SQLite's normal
+  cross-process shared-memory locking, while exclusive mode permits WAL for
+  the kernel's single-owner database capability. Native builds retain Node's
+  normal locking mode.
+- The normal runtime still reports Node 24.13.2. Only the diagnostic build may
+  cross the OpenClaw Node floor until the broader compatibility profile passes.
+
+## Ownership
+
+The implementation belongs to the Edge.js internal-binding layer and build
+graph. OpenClaw remains unmodified. SQLite source identity and browser evidence
+belong to the downstream Clawsembly kernel proof.
